./scripts/local-cleanup.md:5:After fetching and before pulling, the script checks whether local `main` is ahead of `origin/main` only by prior larch-log flush commits. The cleanup is deliberately narrow: every ahead commit subject must begin with the `chore(larch-logs): flush` prefix and the aggregate diff must stay under `larch-logs/`. The diff for that second predicate is evaluated against the pre-fetch `origin/main` tip (captured immediately before `git fetch origin main`) so a just-landed squash-merge cannot contaminate the check with the PR's code files on the updated remote. When both predicates pass, the script warns on stderr and resets local `main` to `origin/main` so stale prior-run flush commits do not block the pull. Non-flush ahead work is left untouched.
