./larch-logs/implement/1F079E79-D8B4-443E-A639-3E079574CAFE/review-findings-full.jsonl:9:{"id":"FINDING_6","issue_number":"2468","phase":"plan-review","outcome":"accepted","reviewer":"panel","round_num":"","category":"Fix-issue NON_PR final-report should fire after Step 6b (close+rename), not Step 5b (work)","prose_body":"## Fix-issue NON_PR final-report should fire after Step 6b (close+rename), not Step 5b (work)\n\n**Concern**: NON_PR closure happens in Step 6b (`issue-lifecycle.sh close` + `tracking-issue-write.sh rename`), not in Step 5b. Posting the `closed-non-pr` summary at Step 5b means the issue isn't actually closed yet when the summary is emitted — a misleading ordering. Raised by 2 reviewers.\n\n**Suggested resolution**: Move the NON_PR `write-final-report.sh` call to after Step 6b close+rename succeeds (and after Step 6c umbrella finalize), before Step 8 cleanup. Write `OUTCOME=closed-non-pr` to `outcome.txt` only after close succeeds. Provide a separate failure outcome if close fails.\n\n---"}
./larch-logs/implement/1F079E79-D8B4-443E-A639-3E079574CAFE/review-findings-full.jsonl:11:{"id":"FINDING_8","issue_number":"2468","phase":"plan-review","outcome":"accepted","reviewer":"panel","round_num":"","category":"classification.txt and pr-capture.txt need explicit durable write steps in SKILL.md","prose_body":"## classification.txt and pr-capture.txt need explicit durable write steps in SKILL.md\n\n**Concern**: The fix-issue `write-final-report.sh` reads from `classification.txt` and `pr-capture.txt`, but these files don't exist today and the plan does not add explicit write steps for them in the SKILL.md edits. The orchestrator currently holds classification as a prompt-side variable. Raised by 5 reviewers.\n\n**Suggested resolution**: Add explicit state-write steps before each report call site. Simplest approach: use a single `$FIX_ISSUE_TMPDIR/final-report-state.sh` file with KV lines for `ISSUE_NUMBER`, `CLASSIFICATION`, `PR_NUMBER`, `PR_URL`, `OUTCOME` — written at the point each value is known (Step 4 for classification, Step 5a success for PR capture, Step 3/5b/0-exits for outcome). The write-final-report.sh sources this file. This is analogous to how `ship-pr-state.sh` works in /implement.\n\n---"}
./larch-logs/implement/1F079E79-D8B4-443E-A639-3E079574CAFE/review-findings-full.jsonl:16:{"id":"FINDING_13","issue_number":"2468","phase":"code-review","outcome":"accepted","reviewer":"cursor-specialist-correctness-output.txt","round_num":"1","category":"correctness","prose_body":"## correctness: skills/fix-issue/scripts/write-final-report.sh:95-177\n\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-correctness-output.txt\n- **Concern**: [important] bailed PR-path outcomes still run GitHub upsert after --print-stdout Step 5a bail sets bailed-implement-failed or bailed-adopted-issue-closed; script posts fix-issue final-summary marker on the tracking issue despite plan terminal-only bail and /implement owning that surface Add bailed-* to skip_upsert (or equivalent branch) so only terminal output runs; align SKILL if needed\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above."}
./larch-logs/implement/1F079E79-D8B4-443E-A639-3E079574CAFE/review-findings-full.jsonl:17:{"id":"FINDING_14","issue_number":"2468","phase":"code-review","outcome":"accepted","reviewer":"cursor-specialist-plan-fidelity-output.txt","round_num":"1","category":"correctness","prose_body":"## correctness: skills/fix-issue/scripts/write-final-report.sh:95-178\n\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-plan-fidelity-output.txt\n- **Concern**: [important] skip_upsert omits bailed-implement-failed and bailed-adopted-issue-closed Step 5a bail paths still upsert fix-issue:final-summary despite plan terminal-only (no GitHub post) requirement Extend skip_upsert (or branch) for both bailed outcomes and add harness coverage proving tracking-issue-summary.sh is not called\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above."}
