./larch-logs/implement/1F079E79-D8B4-443E-A639-3E079574CAFE/session-transcript.jsonl:104:{"turn":103,"role":"assistant","blocks":[{"type":"tool_call","id":"toolu_01NMhZk5vmnXVKfi6bSTiePY","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Design heavy phase: sketches, dialectic, plan, review","prompt":"You are the `/design` heavy worker subagent. Read `<OPERATOR_REPO_PATH>/plugins/cache/larch-local/larch/29.8.54/skills/design/references/heavy-worker.md` FIRST, then follow the procedure defined there.\n\n## Environment\n\n```\nDESIGN_TMPDIR=<TMPDIR>\nIMPLEMENT_TMPDIR=<TMPDIR>\nSESSION_ENV_PATH=<TMPDIR>/session-env.sh\nCLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT=<OPERATOR_REPO_PATH>/plugins/cache/larch-local/larch/29.8.54\nquick_mode=false\nauto_mode=false\ncodex_available=true\ncursor_available=true\nCODEX_PRESENT=true\nCURSOR_PRESENT=true\nCURRENT_BRANCH=sergey-zhupanov/standardize-end-of-run-summary\nIS_MAIN=false\nIS_USER_BRANCH=true\nUSER_PREFIX=sergey-zhupanov\n```\n\n## Feature Description\n\nStandardize end-of-run summary in /implement and /fix-issue. Replace /implement Step 17's improvisational prose with a single write-final-report.sh --print-stdout invocation emitting a rich bullet-list run-summary block; extend write-final-report.sh to compose the full block (Outcome, Mode, Path, Duration, Tokens, Cost, Issue, PR, Plan review, Code review, OOS filed, Exec issues, Warnings, Run logs) sourced from tmpdir state files; add --print-stdout flag for byte-identical terminal + GitHub upsert; add Step 18 hook so bail/stall paths also post the summary; create new skills/fix-issue/scripts/write-final-report.sh with parallel guarantees for the 8 /fix-issue outcome enum values (pr-merged, pr-open, closed-non-pr, closed-not-material, bailed-implement-failed, bailed-adopted-issue-closed, no-candidate, lock-failed); centralize per-vendor cost formatting in scripts/token-cost.sh; introduce LARCH_CLAUDE_RATE_PER_M, LARCH_CODEX_RATE_PER_M, LARCH_CURSOR_RATE_PER_M envs with LARCH_TOKEN_RATE_PER_M as Claude fallback; update summary-comment-template.md, write-final-report.md, /implement SKILL.md Steps 17+18, /fix-issue SKILL.md Steps 3/5a/5b/6a/6b/0-exits; add test harnesses test-write-final-report.sh (implement) and test-write-final-report.sh (fix-issue) wired into make lint; remove branched prose from Steps 17/18. Schema sentinel tail: <!-- larch:run-summary v=1 -->. See issue #2468 for the full spec, format examples, and locked decisions.\n\n## Additional Context\n\nThe issue #2468 in character-ai/larch repo contains the complete spec. Key locked decisions:\n1. Format: single bullet list with bold keys, autolink URLs, code spans for flags/paths, h2 header, HTML sentinel tail\n2. Byte-identical terminal + GitHub upsert\n3. Fire on ALL outcomes including bail/stall\n4. Cost line: `TOTAL ~$X.XX — Claude $X.XX, Codex $X.XX, Cursor $X.XX`\n5. /fix-issue posts to subject issue; PR path skips (implement covers it); no-candidate/lock-failed terminal-only\n6. NON_PR \"Issues filed\" = N/A in v1\n7. Mode-specific Note: lines appear AFTER the byte-identical block\n8. Re-use existing `larch:final-summary` marker (not a new one)\n9. New rate envs: LARCH_CLAUDE_RATE_PER_M, LARCH_CODEX_RATE_PER_M, LARCH_CURSOR_RATE_PER_M\n\nThe `$DESIGN_TMPDIR/run-params.json` is already written with HARD classification, sketch_budget=4, review_budget=full.\nThe `$DESIGN_TMPDIR/feature-description.txt` is already written.\nThe `$DESIGN_TMPDIR/discussion-round1.md` is already written (empty - no scope decisions needed).\nThe branch `sergey-zhupanov/standardize-end-of-run-summary` is already created.\n\nSince `auto_mode=false`, stop after Step 3 (plan review) — do NOT run Step 3b (architecture diagram) or Step 4. The parent `/design` orchestrator will run those steps.\n\nReturn ONLY the KV block at the end. First line MUST be `DESIGN_HEAVY=complete` or `DESIGN_HEAVY=failed REASON=<token>`. No prose in the return."}}]}
./larch-logs/implement/1F079E79-D8B4-443E-A639-3E079574CAFE/session-transcript.jsonl:106:{"turn":105,"role":"assistant","blocks":[{"type":"tool_call","id":"toolu_01D4t2u7SPFzEYxwQ9sk5RmJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"DESIGN_TMPDIR=<TMPDIR>\n# Tier 1 non-empty checks\nfor f in approach-synthesis.txt diff-lines.txt plan.txt voting-tally.md; do\n  if [ -s \"$DESIGN_TMPDIR/$f\" ]; then echo \"OK: $f\"; else echo \"MISSING/EMPTY: $f\"; fi\ndone\n# Tier 2 existence checks\nfor f in contested-decisions.md oos.md rejected-findings.md accepted-plan-findings.md; do\n  if [ -f \"$DESIGN_TMPDIR/$f\" ]; then echo \"OK: $f\"; else echo \"MISSING: $f\"; fi\ndone\n# Check design-summary.json\nif [ -s \"$DESIGN_TMPDIR/design-summary.json\" ]; then echo \"OK: design-summary.json\"; else echo \"MISSING/EMPTY: design-summary.json\"; fi","description":""}}]}
