./larch-logs/implement/3890E7C4-6C5E-4070-BD32-F9974BFA66DB/round-1/dyn-ordering-invariant-output.txt:5:- **architecture** `scripts/ship-pr.sh:1754-1762` + `scripts/larch-log.sh:442-450` — After a successful merge, `write_post_merge_sentinel` creates `$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/post-merge-sentinel` before `postmerge` (`scripts/ship-pr.sh:199-208`, `scripts/ship-pr.md:19`), and `run_postmerge_phase` runs `implement-finalize.sh postmerge` first (`scripts/ship-pr.sh:1689-1691`), which performs `local-cleanup.sh` and `verify-main.sh` so the worktree is normally on the default branch (`scripts/implement-finalize.sh:1086-1120`). The new `larch-log.sh commit` therefore hits `larch-log.sh`’s refusal when the sentinel exists (lines 442-445) and, even if that were absent, the separate refusal on the default branch (lines 447-450). The call is best-effort only via `record_failure`, so production runs will still not land an updated `final-summary.md` on `main`, leaving the original audit problem unresolved while adding recurring warning noise. **Suggested fix:** Teach `larch-log.sh commit` a deliberately narrow, ship-pr-only bypass (or an alternate scoped git commit path) that is allowed only from `run_postmerge_phase` after merge cleanup, with explicit preconditions and path-scoped adds; update `SECURITY.md` and `scripts/ship-pr.md:19-20` so the sentinel story and the new flush stay consistent.
./larch-logs/implement/3890E7C4-6C5E-4070-BD32-F9974BFA66DB/round-1/dyn-ordering-invariant-output.txt:7:- **architecture** `scripts/ship-pr.md:75` vs `scripts/ship-pr.md:89-91` — The doc still states that the post-merge sentinel exists so postmerge cannot create larch-log-only commits on `main`, while the revised Postmerge Phase paragraph promises a post-merge `larch-log.sh commit` on the current branch (typically `main`). That is a direct contract contradiction on the same page. **Suggested fix:** Once the real flush mechanism is decided, rewrite one of these bullets so the sentinel rationale and the intentional post-merge commit path are explicitly reconciled (for example, sentinel continues to block prompt-side/teardown commits while a named, audited exception covers only this single `ship-pr.sh` call).
./larch-logs/implement/3890E7C4-6C5E-4070-BD32-F9974BFA66DB/round-1/dyn-ordering-invariant-output.txt:11:- The diff also adds under `larch-logs/implement/3890E7C4-6C5E-4070-BD32-F9974BFA66DB/` plan/manifest collateral from this implement run; if that was not meant to ship with the functional fix, consider dropping it as unrelated churn before merge.
