./larch-logs/implement/F17F9ABF-B557-43F7-A91C-32CE430C0533/round-1/findings.md:63:- **Concern**: [important] Part A convergence can overwrite fix-applied, main-agent-vote-required, no-changes, etc. Low accept counts after fix-applied can rewrite status to converged-small-changes; Implement Step 5 then skips the fix-applied run-relevant-checks path. Vote-required can be overwritten before adjudication. Only run Part A for intended terminal statuses (e.g. complete); never after fix-applied or main-agent-vote-required.
./larch-logs/implement/F17F9ABF-B557-43F7-A91C-32CE430C0533/round-1/findings.md:108:- **Concern**: [latent] New statuses/keys are not wired into /implement Step 5 loop or launcher. Orchestrator may not stop the loop on converged-small-changes or skip cap accounting for DEGRADED_ROUND as documented. Update Step 5 scripted review loop and launcher/docs to parse and act on these outputs.
./larch-logs/implement/F17F9ABF-B557-43F7-A91C-32CE430C0533/round-1/findings.md:113:- **Concern**: [important] Feature and new doc require degraded rounds not to count toward the implement review round cap, but no consumer reads DEGRADED_ROUND or adjusts round_num toward ROUND_CAP. Degraded panels still advance round_num under Step 5 re-review / bulk-skip gates until round_cap, so cap exhaustion can happen without a valid panel tally—contrary to don't burn round cap. Update Step 5 loop (SKILL and/or run-step5-review.sh) to treat DEGRADED_ROUND=true as not consuming cap (document exact semantics if partial burns are intended).
./larch-logs/implement/F17F9ABF-B557-43F7-A91C-32CE430C0533/round-1/findings.md:118:- **Concern**: [important] Convergence can overwrite fix-applied status after coder commit Low accept counts plus fix-applied commit emit REVIEW_AND_FIX_STATUS=converged-small-changes; Step 5 may skip fix-applied checks path despite repo-changing commit Do not let convergence supersede fix-applied or define explicit combined status + orchestrator handling
./larch-logs/implement/F17F9ABF-B557-43F7-A91C-32CE430C0533/round-1/findings.md:123:- **Concern**: [important] DEGRADED_ROUND is documented for cap and convergence accounting but no orchestrator consumes it in this branch. Degraded rounds still consume the review round cap; behavior diverges from the published contract. Update Step 5 loop or equivalent to read DEGRADED_ROUND and adjust cap or round accounting accordingly.
./larch-logs/implement/3890E7C4-6C5E-4070-BD32-F9974BFA66DB/round-1/dyn-test-stub-coverage-output.txt:4:- **risk-integration** `scripts/test-ship-pr.sh:1315-1368` — The `postmerge_flush` update and new `postmerge_no_logs_commit` case only grep `larch-log-calls.txt` for `manifest` / `status=done` / `LARCH_LOG_ARGS=commit` (or its absence); neither records nor asserts any `write-final-report.sh` invocation, so deleting the new `write-final-report.sh` block in `run_postmerge_phase` would still satisfy these tests as long as `larch-log.sh` runs. The default stub at `scripts/test-ship-pr.sh:111-115` always exits 0 and only prints `STATUS=ok`, so it does not exercise outcome rendering, and because `record_failure` only appends via `append_tool_failure_local` (`scripts/ship-pr.sh:512-521`) while `run_postmerge_phase` still ends with `advance_phase "done"` and `exit 0` (`scripts/ship-pr.sh` tail of `run_postmerge_phase`), a non-zero `write-final-report.sh` exit would not fail the harness unless another assertion inspected `execution-issues.md` or exit status. **Suggested fix:** Teach the shared `write-final-report.sh` stub in `write_stubs` (or a dedicated postmerge fixture) to append a sentinel line such as `WRFR_POSTMERGE_ARGS=...` to `"${LARCH_LOG_STUB_SENTINEL_DIR}/larch-log-calls.txt"` (or a sibling file) when that env is set, mirroring `scripts/test-ship-pr.sh:104-109`, and extend both tests to `grep` for that marker in order between manifest `status=done` and the optional `larch-log.sh commit` line; optionally assert `grep -q '^OUTCOME=merged'` in `$tmp/larch-logs/implement/test-run/final-summary.md` after adding `MERGE_RESULT=merged` to the fixture state in `write_state` for those scenarios.
./larch-logs/implement/3890E7C4-6C5E-4070-BD32-F9974BFA66DB/round-1/dyn-test-stub-coverage-output.txt:7:- The branch diff adds committed implement run metadata under `larch-logs/implement/3890E7C4-6C5E-4070-BD32-F9974BFA66DB/` (plan copy, manifest, etc.), which is unrelated noise next to the functional `ship-pr.sh` change and may complicate review and bisect.
./larch-logs/implement/3890E7C4-6C5E-4070-BD32-F9974BFA66DB/round-1/dyn-test-stub-coverage-output.txt:9:- `postmerge_missing_manifest` (`scripts/test-ship-pr.sh:1371-1396`) uses the same larch-log-only sentinel pattern and likewise does not pin the new `write-final-report.sh` step.
./larch-logs/implement/3890E7C4-6C5E-4070-BD32-F9974BFA66DB/round-1/aggregator-output.txt:4:- **Concern**: After `larch-log.sh manifest`, `run_postmerge_phase` can still run `write-final-report.sh` and (when not suppressed) `larch-log.sh commit` without treating a non-zero manifest exit as a hard stop; `larch-log.sh commit` can also run after `write-final-report.sh` fails because failures are folded into `record_failure` while the phase still advances. That can land a log commit whose tree does not reliably reflect `status=done` plus an updated merged `final-summary.md`, preserving stale `OUTCOME`/summary on failure paths (the original audit-class bug on partial failure). Doc text that reads like strict ordering after manifest reaches `status=done` mismatches this non-aborting control flow.
./larch-logs/implement/3890E7C4-6C5E-4070-BD32-F9974BFA66DB/round-1/aggregator-output.txt:5:- **Suggested revision**: Persist manifest exit status and skip flush/commit unless it is zero; run `larch-log.sh commit` only when `write-final-report.sh` exits zero (or document and test an explicit alternative fail-closed policy); align `scripts/ship-pr.md` narrative with whichever policy is chosen.
./larch-logs/implement/3890E7C4-6C5E-4070-BD32-F9974BFA66DB/round-1/aggregator-output.txt:12:### FINDING_3: Post-merge larch-log commit likely conflicts with sentinel and default-branch refusal
./larch-logs/implement/3890E7C4-6C5E-4070-BD32-F9974BFA66DB/round-1/aggregator-output.txt:14:- **Concern**: Ordering/invariants imply a post-merge sentinel exists before `postmerge`, and `implement-finalize.sh postmerge` leaves the worktree on the default branch; `larch-log.sh commit` is documented to refuse when the sentinel exists and on the default branch, so the new post-merge commit may be best-effort-only via `record_failure`, failing to update `final-summary.md` on `main` while adding recurring warnings—undermining the intended audit fix unless refusal rules and callers are reconciled.
./larch-logs/implement/3890E7C4-6C5E-4070-BD32-F9974BFA66DB/round-1/aggregator-output.txt:17:### FINDING_4: ship-pr.md contradicts itself on post-merge sentinel vs post-merge larch-log commit
./larch-logs/implement/3890E7C4-6C5E-4070-BD32-F9974BFA66DB/round-1/aggregator-output.txt:19:- **Concern**: Interface/State/Invariants still read like the sentinel suppresses post-merge `larch-log` commits (and/or that postmerge cannot create/push larch-log-only commits on `main`) while the Postmerge section documents an intentional post-merge `larch-log.sh commit` on the current branch (typically `main`). Operators and auditors cannot tell which contract is authoritative.
./larch-logs/implement/3890E7C4-6C5E-4070-BD32-F9974BFA66DB/round-1/aggregator-output.txt:27:### FINDING_6: test harness stub does not model real larch-log commit refusal rules
