./larch-logs/implement/F17F9ABF-B557-43F7-A91C-32CE430C0533/round-5/cursor-specialist-edge-cases-output-ns-retry.txt:9:- **Issue**: `convergence_candidate_status` treats `no-changes` (and `in-scope-filtered-out`) like `complete` for the low-accept / two-round heuristic, so two consecutive rounds can each have small `ACCEPTED_COUNT` while reviewers still vote in accepted findings the coder never lands; the script can still emit `REVIEW_AND_FIX_STATUS=converged-small-changes` and `/implement` Step 5 is instructed to stop the re-review loop.
./larch-logs/implement/F17F9ABF-B557-43F7-A91C-32CE430C0533/round-5/cursor-specialist-edge-cases-output-ns-retry.txt:22:- **Location**: [scripts/run-step5-review.sh](scripts/run-step5-review.sh) (`count_prior_degraded_rounds`, argv `--round-cap` inflation ~118–181); [skills/implement/SKILL.md](skills/implement/SKILL.md) (Step 5 gate / `effective_round_cap` narrative ~1324–1328)
./larch-logs/implement/F17F9ABF-B557-43F7-A91C-32CE430C0533/round-5/cursor-specialist-edge-cases-output-ns-retry.txt:23:- **Issue**: Mechanical argv inflation is implemented in `run-step5-review.sh`, while Step 5’s human-facing loop contract also asks the orchestrator to recompute `effective_round_cap` from `DEGRADED_ROUND` plus prior counts; any drift between those recipes (or partial SKILL compliance) yields either premature “hit cap” behavior or extra rounds versus the launcher.
./larch-logs/implement/F17F9ABF-B557-43F7-A91C-32CE430C0533/round-5/cursor-specialist-edge-cases-output-ns-retry.txt:28:1	in_scope	latent	correctness	skills/review-and-fix/scripts/review-and-fix.sh:139-145,1206-1236	convergence_candidate_status includes no-changes/in-scope-filtered-out for two-round low-accept termination	Two rounds in a row can report small ACCEPTED_COUNT while accepted findings keep returning; coder no-changes twice can still yield converged-small-changes and halt Step 5 per SKILL handling.	Narrow convergence to statuses where low accepts truly mean a fixed point (e.g. exclude no-changes when ACCEPTED_COUNT>0) or add an explicit non-convergence guard.
./larch-logs/implement/F17F9ABF-B557-43F7-A91C-32CE430C0533/round-5/findings.md:8:- **Concern**: [latent] Standalone review-and-fix skill doc not updated while implement SKILL documents new statuses/cap math. Operators may miss converged-small-changes and DEGRADED_ROUND semantics when not using /implement Step 5. Add a short cross-reference in skills/review-and-fix/SKILL.md to review-and-fix.md for the new contract fields.
./larch-logs/implement/F17F9ABF-B557-43F7-A91C-32CE430C0533/round-5/findings.md:43:- **Concern**: [important] Stale degraded-retry.flag/.done from an earlier completed run suppresses the one allowed panel retry on a later re-invocation while voting-tally.md can still show the degraded banner after a fresh review-core run. A second Step 5 run reusing the same round-N directory can leave DEGRADED_ROUND=true and skip the extra review-core attempt even though this invocation only executed review-core once and the banner persists. Clear or re-key retry markers at round start or gate skip logic on artifact freshness tied to the current review-core output.
./larch-logs/implement/F17F9ABF-B557-43F7-A91C-32CE430C0533/round-5/findings.md:48:- **Concern**: [nit] New --convergence-threshold flag is not forwarded by the Step 5 launcher. Feature is only reachable for callers that invoke review-and-fix.sh directly unless env wiring is added elsewhere. Optionally plumb a session-env knob into REVIEW_AND_FIX_ARGS or document the limitation explicitly in run-step5-review.md.
./larch-logs/implement/F17F9ABF-B557-43F7-A91C-32CE430C0533/round-5/findings.md:53:- **Concern**: [nit] The Step 5 launcher never passes --convergence-threshold to review-and-fix.sh, so /implement cannot set a non-default threshold via the supported launcher path. Operators who expect session-configurable convergence in implement mode will always get the default unless they bypass the launcher. Optional session-env wiring for the flag, or explicit documentation that the threshold is only for direct/harness invocation.
