./larch-logs/implement/8806AEE0-8D33-4861-AE0D-A78FF2939937/session-transcript.jsonl:223:{"turn":222,"role":"assistant","blocks":[{"type":"text","value":"Evaluating findings. Critical functional regressions:\n1. `git-show-stage.sh:46` — `exec git show` after quiet init sends content to log, not caller stdout (breaks conflict resolution)\n2. `sessionstart-health.sh:114` — jq advisory output goes to quiet log instead of hook stdout\n3. `gh-pr-checks.sh:44` — raw `gh pr checks` diagnostic passthrough goes to quiet log\n4. `pre-commit-shellcheck.sh:40` — shellcheck findings suppressed in pre-commit\n\nLower priority / reject:\n- Single umbrella commit vs A–J groups → reject (style, PR still reviewable)\n- Branch scope includes prior-run larch-logs → reject (existing commits, not new work)\n- `false-positive-keywords.sh` not converted → correct (sourced-only library, audit-only per issue)\n- Widespread `>&2` after init → OOS follow-up, not critical for automated callers\n- Test coverage for quiet mode → OOS\n\nFixing the 4 critical regressions:"}]}
./larch-logs/implement/8806AEE0-8D33-4861-AE0D-A78FF2939937/session-transcript.jsonl:279:{"turn":278,"role":"assistant","blocks":[{"type":"text","value":"`PHASE=done`, `PR_CLOSED=true`, `DONE_RENAME_APPLIED=true`. PR merged successfully.\n\n> **🔶 /implement 16: rejected findings**\n\nRejected findings (not implemented):\n- Single umbrella commit vs A–J commit groups — style preference, PR is reviewable\n- Branch scope includes prior-run larch-logs — pre-existing commits\n- `false-positive-keywords.sh` not converted — correctly excluded (sourced-only library, audit-only per issue)\n- Widespread `>&2` after quiet init → `larch_err` — valid follow-up pattern, filed as OOS below\n\n> **🔶 /implement 17: final report**\n\nPR **https://github.com/character-ai/larch/pull/2133** merged as **27.5.71**."}]}
./larch-logs/implement/0DB4540C-652D-4175-A074-DE570BACD6BB/round-1/review-round-summary.md:11:### FINDING_1: **Important** `risk-integration` `scripts/merge-pr.sh:173-175`, `scripts/git-force-push.sh:43-48`: the new caller classifies local commits against `PR_HEAD_OID`, but `git-force-push.sh` refreshes `origin/$BRANCH` immediately before `--force-with-lease`, so a remote commit pushed after the PR view can be overwritten. Concrete failing scenario: `gh pr view` returns `aaaa1111`, local HEAD is `aaaa1111 + flush`, another process pushes `dddd4444`, then the helper fetches `dddd4444` and the lease permits replacing it with the local flush-only head. Fix by using an explicit expected lease for this recovery path, e.g. a helper option that pushes with `--force-with-lease=refs/heads/$BRANCH:$PR_HEAD_OID`, and bail if the remote no longer equals the PR OID.
./larch-logs/implement/0DB4540C-652D-4175-A074-DE570BACD6BB/round-1/review-round-summary.md:13:- **Concern**: 2. **Important** `risk-integration` `scripts/merge-pr.sh:173-175`, `scripts/git-force-push.sh:43-48`: the new caller classifies local commits against `PR_HEAD_OID`, but `git-force-push.sh` refreshes `origin/$BRANCH` immediately before `--force-with-lease`, so a remote commit pushed after the PR view can be overwritten. Concrete failing scenario: `gh pr view` returns `aaaa1111`, local HEAD is `aaaa1111 + flush`, another process pushes `dddd4444`, then the helper fetches `dddd4444` and the lease permits replacing it with the local flush-only head. Fix by using an explicit expected lease for this recovery path, e.g. a helper option that pushes with `--force-with-lease=refs/heads/$BRANCH:$PR_HEAD_OID`, and bail if the remote no longer equals the PR OID.
./larch-logs/implement/0DB4540C-652D-4175-A074-DE570BACD6BB/round-1/review-round-summary.md:19:- **Concern**: [nit] Batched discovery implies a single gh pr view for OID precondition; flush recovery adds another pr view. API-count or audit assumptions omit the extra round-trip. Note optional second gh pr view on flush recovery.
./larch-logs/implement/0DB4540C-652D-4175-A074-DE570BACD6BB/round-1/review-round-summary.md:47:### FINDING_2: **Important** `risk-integration` `scripts/merge-pr.sh:173-184`, `scripts/merge-pr.sh:247-265`: after force-pushing the flush commits, the script continues using the CI and merge-state result collected for the old PR head. Concrete failing scenario: PR head `aaaa1111` has passing checks, local `cccc3333` is force-pushed by the recovery path, GitHub checks for `cccc3333` are still pending, and line 264 can still run `gh pr merge --squash --admin` based on stale `CI_GOOD=true`. Fix by making recovery restart or re-run the PR metadata and `gh pr checks` gates for the updated `headRefOid` before any merge attempt.
./larch-logs/implement/0DB4540C-652D-4175-A074-DE570BACD6BB/round-1/review-round-summary.md:49:- **Concern**: 1. **Important** `risk-integration` `scripts/merge-pr.sh:173-184`, `scripts/merge-pr.sh:247-265`: after force-pushing the flush commits, the script continues using the CI and merge-state result collected for the old PR head. Concrete failing scenario: PR head `aaaa1111` has passing checks, local `cccc3333` is force-pushed by the recovery path, GitHub checks for `cccc3333` are still pending, and line 264 can still run `gh pr merge --squash --admin` based on stale `CI_GOOD=true`. Fix by making recovery restart or re-run the PR metadata and `gh pr checks` gates for the updated `headRefOid` before any merge attempt.
